es.cessda.eu\/vocabulary\/TopicClassification?v=4.2#Politics.PoliticalBehaviourAndAttitudes"],"expandedvalue":[{"@id":"https:\/\/vocabularies.cessda.eu\/vocabulary\/TopicClassification?v=4.2#Politics.PoliticalBehaviourAndAttitudes","vocabularyUri":"https:\/\/vocabularies.cessda.eu\/vocabulary\/TopicClassification?v=4.2"}]},{"typeName":"dansUniverse","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["Eligible voters in the Dutch Parliamentary elections of 2023"]},{"typeName":"dansFrequencyOfDataCollection","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"One pre-election and two post-election waves"},{"typeName":"dansSamplingProcedureFreeText","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"For the standard DPES2023, a representative sample was drawn from 1. the LISS panel monitored by CenterData and 2. from the non-self subscribe panel from I&O-research.\nFor the extra data collection among voters with a migration background, all remaining panel-members from both panels have been invited to participate\nFor the extra data collection among voters with an education not at hbo\/university level, the members from I&O sample have been invited for participation."},{"typeName":"dansWeighting","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"The standard DPES 2023 includes three different post-stratification survey weights:\n(1) weights only for demographic characteristics (gender, age, region, migration background and generation), for everyone in the dataset.\n(2) weights only for vote choice and non-voting (distribution between the various parties and abstention).\n(3) weights for both demographics and vote choice.\n\nThe additional datasets based on migration background and education do not contain these weights."}]},"dansTemporalSpatial":{"displayName":"Temporal and Spatial Coverage","name":"dansTemporalSpatial","fields":[{"typeName":"dansTemporalCoverage","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["2023"]},{"typeName":"dansSpatialCoverageControlled","multiple"